<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan firms given nod for overseas fund-raising.</title>
<headline>Taiwan firms given nod for overseas fund-raising.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's securities watchdog body said on Wednesday it has given approvals to three local firms to raise a total of US$407 million overseas.</p>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission agreed to let Macronix International Co Ltd and Delta Electronic Industrial Co Ltd issue US$250 million and US$100 million in corporate bonds overseas, respectively, a statement said.</p>
<p>It also gave nod to Accton Technology Corp to issue T$1.56 billion (US$57 million) in global depository receipts overseas, the statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not give further details. (US$1 = T$27.5)</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
